{"agent_id":"pp3g-99G6-re-review-the-revised-154-durable-opencode-silent-de19","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:16:31.074888404Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"a0525546-5166-44b2-8cb0-0021e3698699","comment_uuid":"d501ff0c-8deb-48db-9b72-faf9544e2f5e","author":"pp3g-99G6-re-review-the-revised-154-durable-opencode-silent-de19","content":"# RE-REVIEW VERDICT r3 — #180 revised design (round 2) for #154\n\n**Verdict: CONDITIONAL** — every round-1 blocker/finding (B1–B3, F4–F13, R1–R3) is addressed with a credible design, and my independent source re-derivation confirms the overwhelming majority of the design's claims exactly. Two conditions block a PASS: (1) the F5 turn-level guard's code as written does **not compile** against the pinned effect version (`Stream.timeoutFail` does not exist in effect 4.0.0-beta.83 — verified in the fetched package); (2) matrix test 9b, the only test that exercises the F5 guard, is underspecified and can false-positive via the raw-layer `chunkTimeout`. Four further minor findings (Hunk 4 completeness, a terminal-WARN log off-by-one, a §5.1 causal-premise misattribution, and a pervasive filename typo) are listed below.\n\n**Method**: independent re-derivation. I did NOT read round-1 verdict sub-issues #176/#177/#178 or any other re-review sub-issue. I fetched `anomalyco/opencode` @ **v1.18.13** (the installed pin) and @ v1.18.12 (patch base) fresh, fetched effect **4.0.0-beta.83** (the repo's pinned effect, with its repo patch inspected), and inspected the live installed binary, production config, and retained harness artifacts (`/tmp/opencode-hang-test/`). All source claims below were re-derived, not taken from the change-log.\n\n---\n\n## 1. B1 — BOTH guard copies (provider.ts + aiskd.ts) — CLOSED (one incompleteness)\n\n- **Both guards exist in the pinned source**: `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts` `wrapSSE` L37, guard L40; `packages/core/src/aisdk.ts` `wrapSSE` L26, guard L29. Verified byte-identical between v1.18.12 and v1.18.13 (both files; aisdk.ts = 235 lines, matches the design).\n- **Both copies are patched in the design** (Hunks 1–4) and the dispatcher semantics are correct: SSE → `wrapSSE`, non-SSE → `wrapBodyIdle`, unconfigured → unwrapped (no regression vs the current guard behavior). Absent content-type → non-SSE branch, as claimed.\n- **Reachability evidence independently confirmed**:\n  - v1 path is live for `opencode run`: retained harness logs contain `message=process session.id=...` (processor.ts) and `message=\"llm runtime selected\" llm.runtime=ai-sdk` (llm.ts:271). The `application/json` hang log (`run-json.out`) shows exactly the 2-POST-then-silence signature.\n  - `aisdk.ts` (v2) is consumed only via the v2 plugin AISDK hooks — verified: only `packages/plugin/src/v2/effect/aisdk.ts` and `packages/plugin/src/v2/promise/aisdk.ts` reference it outside core; the v2 `SessionRunner` uses `LLMClient.Service`/`llm.stream(request)` (`session/runner/llm.ts` L97/L232) and routes via `OpenAIResponses.route`/`AnthropicMessages.route`/`OpenAICompatibleChat.route` (`runner/model.ts` L144/151/158) — none touch `aisdk.ts`.\n  - `aiskd.ts` has no `headerTimeout` (verified prepareOptions L82–119), so #144's 4 `ProviderHeaderTimeoutError` entries are v1-only, as claimed.\n- **Live binary state (§0) fully verified**: installed `opencode.exe` = 1.18.13, 180,381,824 bytes, mtime 2026-08-05 22:47; `if(false)return` present **2×** (both copies byte-patched); original guard **0×**; `function dy` (v1) + `function or` (v2) both present; `\"autoupdate\": false` present; production config `chunkTimeout=300000`, `headerTimeout=300000`, `timeout=3600000` on both `opencode` and `opencode-go`, no `bodyIdleTimeout` yet.\n- **FINDING B1-1 (minor, must fix at implementation)**: **Hunk 4 (aisdk.ts) is not final code** — the diff adds a second `AbortController` to the `signals` array but keeps the existing `signals.find(...)` extraction which returns only the *first* controller, and then references `bodyIdleAbortCtl`, which the diff never declares. As written this is a compile error (`cannot find name 'bodyIdleAbortCtl'`) or worse. The design's parenthetical acknowledges the patch \"must be finalised\" — acceptable for a design, but flagging so the implementer does not `git apply` it verbatim. The provider.ts Hunk 2 has no such defect.\n- **FINDING B1-2 (trivial, pervasive)**: the file is **`aisdk.ts`** (\"AI SDK\"); the design misspells it **`aiskd.ts`** everywhere. Harmless to the analysis, but a copy-paste hazard for build/grep/apply commands.\n\n## 2. B2 — Option A' idle-progress deadline + numeric chain — CLOSED\n\n- The `wrapBodyIdle` pull() shape is mechanically identical to the proven `wrapSSE` per-read timer (one timer per `pull`, cleared on read resolve), so idle-progress semantics (\"timer resets on every chunk; slow-but-progressing body never aborted\") are correct. F2 (hy3) preserved; Option B's new false-abort class (long streaming bodies labelled non-SSE) correctly documented and rejected.\n- **Numeric chain verified**: `bodyIdleTimeout=600_000` (10 min) × ≤3 POSTs = 30 min worst case to terminal ERROR < request `timeout` 3_600_000 (60 min) < operator timeout. Arithmetic holds. `bodyAbsoluteTimeout=3_300_000` (55 min) default OFF, correctly placed below the 60-min request timeout.\n- `wrapBodyIdle` lifecycle (F7): `settled` guard, `clearTimeout` on `done`, `clearTimeout` in `cancel`, `.catch` on the cancel promise — all correct. One inherited edge (also present in stock `wrapSSE`): `cancel()` does `await reader.cancel(reason)` which could itself hang on a fully-stalled socket; non-blocking, pre-existing.\n\n## 3. B3 — error-class-scoped retry budget + off-by-one — CLOSED (control flow correct; one log-field off-by-one)\n\n- **Unbounded schedule verified**: `SessionRetry.policy()` (retry.ts:176–198) is `Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata` with no recurs cap; `if (!retry) return Cause.done(meta.attempt)` is the only stop.\n- **`meta.attempt` semantics verified against effect source** (effect 4.0.0-beta.83 `dist/Schedule.js` `metadataFn`): `attempt: ++n` with `n` starting at 0 → first retry decision has attempt = 1. `delay(1) = 2000 × 2^0 = 2000 ms`. This is confirmed by the retained harness data (POST gaps 17:55:45→50→57→18:56:08 ≈ 5/7/11 s = 3 s chunkTimeout + 2/4/8 s delays) and by the upstream `retry.test.ts` (\"caps delay at 30 seconds\" → `[2000,4000,8000,16000,30000,…]`; \"policy updates retry status\" → attempt 2 after two steps).\n- **Off-by-one: the design's control-flow claim is CORRECT** — `RETRY_MAX_RETRIES = 2`, stop at `meta.attempt > 2` ⇒ initial + 2 retries = exactly 3 POSTs. The #175 formulation (`RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3`, stop at `>3`) would indeed have produced 4 POSTs. `Cause.done` from the step stops the retry and the effect fails with the last error → `Effect.catch(halt)` → visible ERROR + idle (verified the retry driver: `Pull.catchDone(loop, out => orElse(lastError, out))` with `effect.fail`).\n- **Error-class codes verified**: `ResponseStreamError.name = \"ProviderResponseStreamError\"`, `HeaderTimeoutError.name = \"ProviderHeaderTimeoutError\"` (provider/error.ts); message-v2.ts:625/653/665 map ECONNRESET/HeaderTimeoutError/ResponseStreamError to `APIError { isRetryable: true, metadata: { code: e.name } }`. The proposed bounded class `{ProviderResponseStreamError, ProviderHeaderTimeoutError, ECONNRESET}` is exactly matchable via `metadata.code`.\n- **retry-after preservation verified**: `delay()` honors `retry-after-ms`/`retry-after` seconds/HTTP-date, caps only at `RETRY_MAX_DELAY`; upstream test \"uses retry-after values even when exceeding 10 minutes with headers\" exists and passes unchanged under the design (no metadata.code on plain APIErrors → unbounded path). `retryable()` builds the FreeUsageLimitError/GoUsageLimitError upsell payloads as claimed. Note: bounding ECONNRESET in the tight class is a judgment call (transient network resets might deserve header honoring) — documented, acceptable.\n- **FINDING B3-1 (minor)**: the terminal budget-exhausted WARN's field `total POSTs: meta.attempt + 1` is itself off by one. At the budget stop the deciding attempt is 3 (stop condition `attempt > 2`), and POSTs already performed = initial + 2 retries = **3 = meta.attempt**. The formula prints 4 — the exact off-by-one the design is supposed to eliminate, now in the operator-facing log. Should be `meta.attempt`.\n\n## 4. F4 — per-attempt retry WARN + grep-asserted ERROR — CLOSED\n\n- Placement inside `policy()`'s step (retry.ts:186–196) is correct; the log's `code:` extraction (`SessionV1.APIError.isInstance(error) ? error.data.metadata?.code ?? ...`) is feasible: `isInstance` is a name check (`NamedError.hasName`), which works on the parsed `toObject()` output; `metadata.code` is present on the timeout/stream class. Verified.\n- Grep-asserted acceptance (matrix test 13) is sound: harness logs emit structured `level=WARN`/`level=ERROR` lines, so `grep`-assertion is implementable.\n- The zero-ERROR gap is real (retained `run-json.out` has no ERROR lines), and `halt()` (processor.ts:599) becomes reachable once the budget bounds the schedule — verified the driver flow.\n\n## 5. F5 — turn-level parsed-stream guard + instrumentation + real-provider capture — CONDITIONAL\n\n- **Source claims verified**: llm.ts:271 (`llm runtime selected`), llm.ts:283 (`Effect.logError(\"stream error\")` bridge), llm.ts:323 (`maxRetries: input.retries ?? 0`), llm.ts:371–377 (`Stream.fromAsyncIterable(result.result.fullStream, …)` with no deadline — confirmed the exact consumption site, and `input.retries` is never set anywhere in the session path, so the AI-SDK second layer is 0 for the hang path: F9 confirmed).\n- **FINDING F5-1 (condition, must fix)**: **`Stream.timeoutFail({ duration, error })` does not exist in effect 4.0.0-beta.83.** I grepped the entire fetched effect package: the Stream module has only `Stream.timeout(duration)` (silently *ends* the stream) and `Stream.timeoutOrElse({ duration, orElse })` (switches to a fallback stream). The design's snippet as written will not compile. The correct, verified-available mechanism is `Stream.timeoutOrElse({ duration: Duration.millis(llmIdleTimeout), orElse: () => Stream.fail(new ProviderError.ResponseStreamError(...)) })` — its documented per-pull idle semantics (\"The timeout is checked for each pull\") implement exactly the required \"resets per parsed event\". The fix is mechanical, which is why this is CONDITIONAL and not FAIL, but the current text is not an executable patch.\n- **FINDING F5-2 (condition, must fix)**: **matrix test 9b is underspecified and can false-positive.** If the \"parsed-stream stall\" server stops sending raw bytes, the raw-layer `wrapSSE` `chunkTimeout` (3000 in the harness) fires *before* the turn-level guard — the test would pass via the raw layer and prove nothing about F5. The design's own text admits \"raw chunks keep arriving or not\". The test must pin: SSE headers + SSE comment keepalives (`: ping\\n\\n` or equivalent raw bytes that the AI SDK parser discards) so raw cadence continues while *parsed* events stop — plus a short `llmIdleTimeout` value (the default 600 000 ms would make the test take 10 minutes).\n- **FINDING F5-3 (minor, reasoning)**: §5.1's causal premise — \"the overall timeout (1 h) fires on a stalled raw body (#145 proved it at 15 s)\" — is not established. The retained harness runs opencode under a **shell-level GNU `timeout`** (verified `/tmp/opencode-11813-verify/run-test.sh`: `timeout \"$OUTER\" … opencode run`; EXIT=124 is GNU timeout's code), and the retained `run-json.out` shows no \"operation timed out\" message — the log simply ends. #144's verdict explicitly asserts the opposite (\"the overall timeout … fails to abort the already-resolved response body read\"). The turn-level guard remains justified as defense-in-depth (it fires on parsed-event stall regardless of raw-layer state, so it covers both interpretations), but the design should say so rather than cite the misattributed harness kill.\n- Instrumentation + real-provider capture (test 15) are well-placed and feasible.\n\n## 6. F6–F12 — CLOSED (all source claims verified)\n\n- **F6**: pull()-shape backpressure verified against the stock `wrapSSE`; the #175 eager `start()`/`for(;;)` loop (unbounded buffering) is gone.\n- **F7**: `settled` guard / `clearTimeout` on done+cancel / `.catch` on cancel promise all correct.\n- **F8**: opt-in pattern matches `chunkTimeout` exactly (`false`/`0`/absent → no wrapping); gzip (10) and non-chat (11) tests added.\n- **F9**: `maxRetries: input.retries ?? 0` verified; `input.retries` unset in the session path; POST-count invariant (test 14) is the right observable.\n- **F10**: stage + same-fs `mv` with backup rotation = the #145-proven atomic pattern; rollback symmetric.\n- **F11**: all build claims verified — root `packageManager: \"bun@1.3.14\"`; root `postinstall: \"bun run --cwd packages/core fix-node-pty\"`; the bun-version enforcement lives in `packages/script/src/index.ts` (`semver.satisfies(process.versions.bun, \"^1.3.14\")`), imported via `@opencode-ai/script`; `--skip-embed-web-ui` exists (build.ts L24) with the TUI/`opencode run` unaffected by it (web UI is a separate embedded bundle); workspace-root install is correct for bun workspaces.\n- **F12**: fork-identity marker chain verified end-to-end: `OPENCODE_VERSION`/`OPENCODE_CHANNEL` env → `Script.version`/`Script.channel` (packages/script/src/index.ts) → build.ts defines (L194/L198) → `InstallationVersion = OPENCODE_VERSION` (packages/core/src/installation/version.ts) → `opencode --version`. Drift detection in the wrapper + watcher is a sound design. The `bun-v1.3.14` install-flag caveat is appropriately hedged.\n- **F13**: step-0 stopgap verified live (both copies byte-patched, `autoupdate:false`).\n\n## 7. R2/R3 — CLOSED\n\n- **R2**: test-6 parameters fixed and now discriminating — `SLOW_CHUNK_MS=5000`, 5 chunks, `chunkTimeout=3000`, `bodyIdleTimeout=30000` ⇒ gaps (5 s) **exceed** `chunkTimeout` (3 s), so Option A would false-abort and A' passes; #175's contradictory 2 s < 3 s params are gone. 6b (never completes) correctly bounds the deadline.\n- **R3**: `PER_REQUEST` mode is a genuine addition (harness `server.js` currently has only global modes 0/1/2, no per-request differentiation — verified); test 7 (req 1 hangs, req 2 healthy) covers the F4 concern; the source-confirmed downgrade is accurate — provider.ts:1746 constructs `new AbortController()` inside the per-call fetch closure (verified), so the test is a regression guard.\n\n## 8. Verification matrix sufficiency — SUFFICIENT with the noted exceptions\n\nTests 1–15 map to every finding: 1/2/13/14 → B3+F4; 3 → headerTimeout untouched; 4/5 → no regression; 6/6b/9 → B2 (idle vs total, F2 preserved, stalled-but-not-dead); **9b → F5 (needs pinning per F5-2)**; 10/11 → F8; 12 → F6/F7/B1 unit coverage; 15 → F5 instrumentation; §7.4 covers r2's wrapper-survival, consumer-cancellation, and exit-code checks. Gaps: (a) the v2 `aisdk.ts` copy has no *runtime* test — inherent given its documented unreachability on our path, but the design should state explicitly that the v2 copy is verified by unit test + grep only; (b) the `opencode run` non-zero exit on session error remains an assumption (the design correctly flags it in §7.4).\n\n---\n\n## Verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\nThe revision closes every round-1 finding in substance, and my independent source re-derivation validated the design's key technical claims — the two-guard coverage, the Option A' idle semantics, the 1-based `meta.attempt` off-by-one analysis (verified against effect's actual `++n` metadata counter), the error-class codes, the retry-after preservation, the build/pin/marker chain, and the live-binary §0 state. It is not PASS because two items would fail or mislead at implementation as written:\n\n1. **F5-1**: `Stream.timeoutFail` does not exist in effect 4.0.0-beta.83 — the turn-level guard must be implemented with `Stream.timeoutOrElse({ duration, orElse: () => Stream.fail(...) })` (verified available with per-pull idle semantics).\n2. **F5-2**: test 9b must pin the SSE-comment keepalive mechanism and a short `llmIdleTimeout`; as written it can pass via the raw-layer `chunkTimeout` and falsely \"verify\" the F5 guard.\n\nPlus three minor corrections: **B1-1** (Hunk 4 must be finalized — declare `bodyIdleAbortCtl` and keep both controllers), **B3-1** (terminal-WARN `total POSTs: meta.attempt + 1` should be `meta.attempt`), **F5-3** (§5.1 should attribute the 15 s harness kill to the shell GNU `timeout`, not `AbortSignal.timeout`, and justify the turn-level guard as covering stall at any layer), and the **aiskd.ts/aisdk.ts** filename typo. None of these changes the architecture; all are implementer-level fixes. Re-review after these corrections should re-check only F5 and the two log/controller nits.","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:16:31.068308072Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:kbIWg5NsLQ9H3SqKELHfd64h5u1LjJBiSdK8t6qDW6s","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVozFY5IgL+ZqH7vhdBcOfrW4Xb3KS1Q5VtNxDQuUtnAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJDgN+tEKoRERZtMLJJLowMtEAcSA88GbBJcBTc4xY97TZmUP52Hr0a77QIcLtOgfu1y9joPRt0fUYMnnlS3UDQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:kbIWg5NsLQ9H3SqKELHfd64h5u1LjJBiSdK8t6qDW6s","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgVozFY5IgL+ZqH7vhdBcOfrW4Xb3KS1Q5VtNxDQuUtnAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBpfq4o9SrQw63Lv8o8yb9uQNOpIyL1udeGwuh4bUGa0DL/DCaWbLKDDbMEZFFXHDxrLeW1dKT+F+5yTcZ9kzQs="}
